      "created_at": "2026-03-15T19:15:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-15T19:15:56Z",
      "body": "ok I think you're right that I had a thread racing exit, I thought that wasn't possible as it's a non-daemon thread but this is a mixed rust/python codebase and [I called exit from the rust side](https://github.com/rust-windowing/winit/issues/2698), which maybe doesn't give python a chance to join the threads.\n\nI assume free-threading surfaced this because my call to exit() was previously running with the gil held, preventing unrelated python threads from running during/after libc atexit.\n\nThis gives me the segfault pretty reliably (we don't need a big hmac, we need a lot of calls to hmac so it runs in the window after libctx being freed)\n```python\nimport ctypes\nimport hmac\nimport threading\n\ndef w():\n    while True:\n        hmac.digest(b\"key\", b\"x\", \"sha256\")\n\nfor i in range(8):\n    threading.Thread(target=w).start()\n\nlib = ctypes.cdll.LoadLibrary(\"libc.dylib\")\nlib.exit()\n```",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
